GET - GP NO

In Telangana (rural areas), a Grama Panchayat (GP) layout approved copy and GP Approval Number (GP No.) can be obtained through the following ways 👇

1️⃣ From the Grama Panchayat Office (Main & Most Reliable)
Visit the concerned Grama Panchayat office where the layout is located.
Documents to carry:


Layout name & survey numbers
Village, Mandal, District details
Sale deed / link documents (if available)
Plot number (if applicable)

Ask for:
Layout Approval Proceedings Copy
GP Resolution Number / Approval Number (GP No.)


Date of approval
👉 They will give:


Xerox / certified copy
GP seal & signature (if requested)



2️⃣ From Panchayat Secretary
Contact the Panchayat Secretary directly.


They maintain layout approval registers

Can trace approval using:
Survey number
Layout name

They can issue:
Certified copy
Letter confirming GP approval details





3️⃣ From Mandal Parishad / MPDO Office (If Old Records)
If the layout approval is old (5–15+ years):
Visit MPDO (Mandal Parishad Development Office)


Ask for:
GP layout approval records
Panchayat resolutions archive





4️⃣ From Layout Developer / Plot Owners Association
If the layout was developed by a promoter:


Ask the developer or association
Usually they have:
GP approved layout copy


Approval proceedings with GP No.
⚠️ Always cross-check with GP office for authenticity.

5️⃣ Online – Is It Available?
Currently:
❌ No common public portal for GP layout approvals in Telangana
GP approvals are mostly offline records
(Some new Panchayats may upload records internally, but public access is rare.)

How GP Approval Number Looks
Example formats:
GP/Resolution No: 12/2016
Proceedings No: GP/VLG/Layouts/45/2019
Resolution Date is very important for legal verification



Important Tip ⚠️
Before buying or constructing:
Verify GP approval + ROR (1B) + Layout plan
Ensure land is non-assigned & non-government
GP approval ≠ DTCP approval (valid only for rural areas)



