🏗️ Construction Permission – What You Need (Rural GP Area)

For house construction, GP permission is usually sufficient if the land is valid.

Documents Required:
GP approved layout copy (2013)
GP Resolution / Approval No.
Registered Sale Deed
EC (latest)

ROR-1B / Pattadar Passbook
House plan (by licensed engineer)
Property tax receipt (if already assessed)
👉 Submit these to Aloor-1 GP for:
Building permission
House number allocation

⚠️ Important Legal Checks (Must Do Before Construction)

✔ Confirm land is:
Not assigned land
Not government / poramboke
Not under road / nala / buffer zone
Not in HMDA master plan road alignment

✔ Check:
Survey number matches in sale deed + layout plan
Roads shown in layout are left open

🔎 Extra Safety Tip (Recommended)
Get a legal opinion or verify at:
Sub-Registrar Office, Chevella
Old Encumbrance details
Any GP cancellation resolutions after 2013

